WEBVTT

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.687
Are you sure this rice
isn't supposed to be cooked?

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.193
Steamed, fried?

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.786
The idea is to shower
the couple with a symbol

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:34.300
of good fortune, not garnish
them like a roast chicken.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:36.964
Smile.

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:41.965
Rice, anyone?

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.475
I'll take one.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.307
Red Alert.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.680
Ready?

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.353
This is it, Tom.

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.397
Your bachelor days are over.

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.931
Not a moment too soon.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.933
Second thoughts?

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.868
Second, third, fourth...

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.807
I never thought I'd see the day.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.779
Given the volatile nature

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.839
of their relationship,
one might have

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.181
predicted homicide
rather than matrimony.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.948
When it comes to affairs
of the human heart,

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.250
it is wise to look beyond logic.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.684
We're gathered here today

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:39.960
not as Starfleet officers,
but as friends and family

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:44.527
to celebrate the marriage
of two of Voyager's finest.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:49.541
B'Elanna has asked me to forego
the rigors of Klingon painstiks

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:52.305
in favor of a more
traditional ceremony.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.369
They're saving the painstiks
for the honeymoon.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:57.342
As Captain,

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.853
the honor of joining these
two people has fallen to me,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.445
but before I declare them
husband and wife,

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:06.390
Tom and B'Elanna
have prepared their own vows.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.660
I still don't know what
I've done to deserve you...

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:21.939
but whatever it is,
I'll try to keep doing it,

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:25.511
and I promise to stand by you,

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:28.479
to honor you...

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.948
till death do us part.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.281
Ensign.

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:34.513
Hmm?

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:35.554
The ring.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:36.680
Oh.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:46.426
May this ring be a symbol
of our eternal love.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.263
You stood by me...

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:55.304
when most people would have
run for the nearest airlock.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:03:01.177
You were willing to see past
my shortcomings...

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.841
and to take
all the bumps and bruises

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.578
that came along with it.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.483
You made me a better person...

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.117
even though I put up
one hell of a fight.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:18.256
I look forward
to our journey together.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.462
Commander.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:32.642
May this ring be the symbol
of our eternal love.

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:36.480
Not so fast.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.609
Lieutenant
Thomas Eugene Paris...

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.621
Lieutenant B'Elanna Torres,

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.624
with the power vested in me
by Starfleet Command

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:48.286
and the United
Federation of Planets,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:52.855
I now pronounce you
husband and wife.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.626
Now, Tom.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:02.730
Bravo.

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:16.353
Congratulations.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.582
For what?

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.181
You may not want to know.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:07.448
Captain's Log, Stardate 52586.3.

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:09.392
We've had a lot
to celebrate lately...

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:12.363
Tom and B'Elanna's wedding,
Ensign Harper's new baby

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.992
and the continued health
of our enhanced warp drive,

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:18.434
which has taken us within
striking distance of home.

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.064
In this case, the shortest path
is a straight line.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.074
We'll pass right through
the center of the Milky Way.

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.666
And be in Sector 001
within two years.

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:26.177
More or less.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:28.805
You had Seven double-check
the calculations?

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:30.075
Two years, 11 days, six hours,

00:07:30.149 --> 00:07:32.743
provided we continue to operate
at peak efficiency.

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:33.911
Naturally.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.386
Of course, if we operate
at peak efficiency,

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:38.890
we'll be missing some
interesting phenomena

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.220
along the way...

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:44.161
an anomalous gradient
to the curvature of space,

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.664
unusual bioharmonic readings
from a binary system

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.097
we'll reach
about six months from now.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:50.658
And the scientist in you can't
resist stopping to take a look.

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:52.704
It would only add another
two or three months.

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.330
Do you think
the crew would mutiny?

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:55.374
On the contrary.

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:56.840
Everyone'll jump at the chance

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.501
for some last-minute
exploration.

00:07:58.578 --> 00:07:59.510
Everyone...

00:07:59.579 --> 00:08:01.046
except Seven.

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:02.580
Let your First Officer

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:05.412
deal with
the personnel problems.

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:06.816
Here's a lovely program

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:08.649
modeled
after a mountain resort

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:10.746
on the fifth moon of Cytrax...

00:08:10.823 --> 00:08:13.223
just you, B'Elanna
and the crickets.

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:14.384
Crickets?

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.893
Cytraxian crickets.

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:21.195
Their song is reputed to be
an auditory aphrodisiac.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.531
Aha. Well, between you and me...

00:08:23.603 --> 00:08:26.231
B'Elanna and I
don't need aphrodisiacs.

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:32.433
There's always the beaches
of Ahmedeen... windsurfing

00:08:32.512 --> 00:08:33.843
on a sea of liquid argon.

00:08:33.913 --> 00:08:37.110
I was hoping for someplace
a little more down-to-earth.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.616
Well, it's your honeymoon.

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:40.083
Just how down-to-earth
did you mean?

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:41.210
Earth.

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:43.050
I was thinking

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:45.147
Chicago in the roaring '20s...

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:48.250
speakeasies, flappers,
the Charleston.

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:50.386
If that's what you want.

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:51.794
Why? Is there a problem?

00:08:51.864 --> 00:08:53.331
No, of course not,
it's just that we're

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:54.661
so close to Earth anyway,

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.861
I thought you might want to try
something a little more exotic.

00:08:56.936 --> 00:08:59.734
Let me let you in
on a little secret, Neelix.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:02.797
Earth has the best vacation
spots in the galaxy.

00:09:02.875 --> 00:09:05.002
It's got the cultures,
the climates,

00:09:05.077 --> 00:09:06.567
the history, the people.

00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:09.809
It has everything
you ever want in a planet.

00:09:09.882 --> 00:09:11.782
You sound
like a travel brochure.

00:09:12.919 --> 00:09:15.410
No. No. Just a native.

00:09:15.488 --> 00:09:17.513
Oh, and make sure
the deuterium manifold's

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.387
are never opened wider
than 600 microns.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:21.187
I am familiar
with the specifications.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.057
Are you familiar
with how temperamental

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:24.528
the isolytic converter can be?

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:25.859
Yes.

00:09:25.932 --> 00:09:28.662
Most important,
the enhanced warp drive...

00:09:28.734 --> 00:09:30.998
with the dilithium matrix
running hot all the time now,

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.435
you have to watch it
like a hawk.

00:09:32.505 --> 00:09:34.097
There is no point
in providing me

00:09:34.173 --> 00:09:35.765
with knowledge
I already possess.

00:09:36.842 --> 00:09:38.810
I guess I am being
a little overcautious.

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:42.279
I've just, uh, never
been away from Engineering

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:44.509
for more
than a couple of days...

00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:46.245
certainly never a week.

00:09:46.319 --> 00:09:48.913
My engineering abilities
are more than sufficient.

00:09:49.055 --> 00:09:50.420
Enjoy your honeymoon.

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:53.720
You may understand
the iso-dynamics of this engine,

00:09:53.793 --> 00:09:56.921
but I don't think
you understand its personality.

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:58.291
Personality.

00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:00.525
It is a propulsion device.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.931
That's my point.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:03.467
It's not just a device.

00:10:03.536 --> 00:10:06.198
It-it has its own quirks,
its own... its own moods.

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:11.206
That's just a minor fluctuation
in a subsidiary injector port.

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:12.539
I will take care of it.

00:10:12.612 --> 00:10:14.045
I'm going with you.

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:15.842
Lieutenant, you are on leave.

00:10:15.915 --> 00:10:17.610
Not for another 20 minutes.

00:10:23.422 --> 00:10:25.890
So, who's the lucky guy?

00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:27.289
You caught the bouquet.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.590
That means you're next
in line for the altar.

00:10:29.662 --> 00:10:31.323
Yes, the Doctor informed me

00:10:31.397 --> 00:10:33.592
of that archaic
human superstition.

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:35.725
How about Harry Kim?

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:39.259
I fail to see the benefit
of monogamous relationships.

00:10:39.338 --> 00:10:41.169
So you want to stay single?

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.208
If you mean remain open
to social situations

00:10:43.275 --> 00:10:44.799
with a wide variety
of individuals,

00:10:44.877 --> 00:10:45.935
then yes.

00:10:46.012 --> 00:10:47.775
I'm married...
I'm not going into stasis

00:10:47.847 --> 00:10:49.075
for the rest of my life.

00:10:49.148 --> 00:10:50.410
No, I plan to have...

00:10:50.483 --> 00:10:52.508
I do not wish to be
dependent on anyone.

00:10:52.585 --> 00:10:55.213
By marrying, one limits
one's romantic interactions

00:10:55.287 --> 00:10:56.515
to a single individual...

00:10:56.589 --> 00:10:58.955
a circumstance which
implies extreme monotony.

00:10:59.025 --> 00:11:00.754
I'm glad we had
this little talk.

00:11:03.496 --> 00:11:05.589
Try the manual release.

00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:12.732
I thought you said
it was a minor fluctuation.

00:11:13.773 --> 00:11:15.707
This entire Jefferies tube

00:11:15.775 --> 00:11:17.572
is losing
molecular cohesion.

00:11:17.643 --> 00:11:19.941
I guess the honeymoon's off.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:22.747
It's our warp field.

00:11:22.815 --> 00:11:25.079
The enhanced drive is emitting

00:11:25.151 --> 00:11:26.948
some form
of subspace radiation

00:11:27.019 --> 00:11:29.249
that's affecting
Voyager's infrastructure.

00:11:29.321 --> 00:11:30.720
It's beginning to break down

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.417
the molecular bonds
in all surrounding sections.

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:34.925
We're seeing
early stages of the effect

00:11:34.994 --> 00:11:35.926
in the warp core...

00:11:35.995 --> 00:11:37.929
reaction chamber,
injector ports...

00:11:37.997 --> 00:11:39.624
they're all showing signs
of de-cohesion.

00:11:39.699 --> 00:11:41.064
It doesn't make any sense.

00:11:41.133 --> 00:11:42.725
We knew all about
the subspace radiation

00:11:42.802 --> 00:11:44.064
and we ran
dozens of simulations

00:11:44.136 --> 00:11:46.764
before we brought the new drive
on line.

00:11:46.839 --> 00:11:49.171
Have you tried taking
the core off-line?

00:11:49.241 --> 00:11:51.334
It's not stopping the problem.

00:11:53.012 --> 00:11:54.673
Try to isolate
the cause of this.

00:11:54.747 --> 00:11:57.944
And stabilize the sections
that have already been affected.

00:11:58.017 --> 00:11:59.575
Dismissed.

00:12:13.632 --> 00:12:14.894
Computer.

00:12:14.967 --> 00:12:18.596
Begin Chief Engineer's Log,
supplemental.

00:12:20.973 --> 00:12:23.737
I've spent the last four hours

00:12:23.809 --> 00:12:27.609
analyzing
the warp field schematics,

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.911
but I'm still no closer to
finding out what's going wrong.

00:12:34.487 --> 00:12:36.921
Computer, did it
just get colder in here?

00:12:36.989 --> 00:12:39.253
Negative.

00:12:39.325 --> 00:12:42.488
Raise the temperature
by five degrees.

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:00.644
Hungry?

00:13:00.713 --> 00:13:02.203
Ah, can't join you tonight...

00:13:02.281 --> 00:13:03.543
dinner with B'Elanna.

00:13:03.616 --> 00:13:06.380
Married one day
and you're already domesticated.

00:13:06.452 --> 00:13:07.885
Jealous?

00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:09.147
Night, Harry.

00:13:10.723 --> 00:13:12.554
B'Elanna?

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:14.354
If we're going to live together,

00:13:14.426 --> 00:13:17.554
we're going to have to
compromise on the temperature.

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:21.225
Computer, reset environmental
controls to standard.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.289
B'Elanna?

00:13:32.278 --> 00:13:33.711
Shh.

00:13:35.514 --> 00:13:36.776
Bring her in, quickly.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:40.011
It looks like we've got
an epidemic on our hands.

00:13:58.737 --> 00:14:00.261
Acute cellular degradation?

00:14:00.339 --> 00:14:02.068
Their chromosomes
are breaking down

00:14:02.141 --> 00:14:03.665
at the molecular level.

00:14:03.742 --> 00:14:05.642
Proximity to the warp field.

00:14:05.711 --> 00:14:07.076
I believe so.

00:14:07.146 --> 00:14:08.909
B'Elanna
and my other three patients

00:14:09.048 --> 00:14:10.276
all work in Engineering.

00:14:10.349 --> 00:14:12.817
They've been subjected
to the heaviest exposure,

00:14:12.885 --> 00:14:14.352
but preliminary scans suggest

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:16.911
the rest of the crew has
been affected as well...

00:14:17.056 --> 00:14:18.717
including the Captain.

00:14:18.791 --> 00:14:22.056
It's only a matter of time
before you begin

00:14:22.127 --> 00:14:23.560
showing the same symptoms.

00:14:25.064 --> 00:14:27.191
We've shut down the warp drive,

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:29.791
but the ship is
still deteriorating,

00:14:29.869 --> 00:14:31.666
and so are we.

00:14:31.737 --> 00:14:33.204
Why?

00:14:37.676 --> 00:14:40.577
Every bulkhead and conduit
from Deck 1 to 15

00:14:40.646 --> 00:14:42.876
show signs
of molecular de-cohesion.

00:14:42.948 --> 00:14:45.712
Even food from the replicator
shows signs of decay.

00:14:45.784 --> 00:14:46.944
As soon as anything
comes into contact

00:14:47.052 --> 00:14:48.952
with Voyager's atmosphere,
it's affected.

00:14:49.054 --> 00:14:50.282
That's what we
thought at first,

00:14:50.356 --> 00:14:51.687
but take a look at this.

00:14:51.757 --> 00:14:54.123
These vegetables are
completely free of decay.

00:14:54.193 --> 00:14:55.421
I thought you said
the replicators...

00:14:55.494 --> 00:14:56.756
They weren't replicated.

00:14:56.829 --> 00:14:59.389
I harvested them
on an away mission last week.

00:14:59.465 --> 00:15:01.899
The same goes
for these particle accelerators,

00:15:01.967 --> 00:15:04.629
the trilithium ore samples,
the keg of Hazari ale.

00:15:04.703 --> 00:15:06.603
All of them were brought aboard
over the last few months

00:15:06.672 --> 00:15:08.902
and none of them
is disintegrating.

00:15:08.974 --> 00:15:11.033
We haven't been able to narrow
the time frame precisely,

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:12.907
but it appears that anything

00:15:13.012 --> 00:15:15.742
brought onboard over the past
30 to 40 weeks is immune.

00:15:15.814 --> 00:15:17.577
Something happened
to the ship months ago

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.140
that's causing this decay.

00:15:19.218 --> 00:15:21.015
A logical conclusion.

00:15:22.121 --> 00:15:24.089
Eight months, 17 days ago...

00:15:24.156 --> 00:15:25.885
first contact with the Kmada.

00:15:25.958 --> 00:15:28.085
They tried to sabotage
our life-support systems

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.185
with low-frequency
theta radiation.

00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:33.231
Any chance that could have
caused the phenomenon?

00:15:33.299 --> 00:15:34.459
Unlikely.

00:15:34.533 --> 00:15:35.830
Let's keep looking.

00:15:35.901 --> 00:15:37.926
The next event of note
took place

00:15:38.003 --> 00:15:40.563
nine months, two days ago
when the N'Kree

00:15:40.639 --> 00:15:43.802
tried to conscript Voyager
into their battle fleet.

00:15:43.876 --> 00:15:45.036
And failed.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.634
Next?

00:16:10.769 --> 00:16:12.498
Hey.

00:16:12.571 --> 00:16:15.005
Hey.

00:16:17.009 --> 00:16:19.170
How's my old lady?

00:16:21.347 --> 00:16:23.406
Well enough...

00:16:23.482 --> 00:16:26.383
to break your nose if
you call me that again.

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:33.857
Here it is.

00:16:33.926 --> 00:16:35.527
What?

00:16:39.898 --> 00:16:41.957
Our honeymoon.

00:16:43.602 --> 00:16:44.830
Tell me.

00:16:50.576 --> 00:16:53.943
Six days and seven nights...

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:56.570
in the historic Graystone Hotel

00:16:56.648 --> 00:17:00.243
in beautiful downtown
Chicago, circa 1928.

00:17:06.392 --> 00:17:09.555
Uh, wait till you see it...

00:17:09.628 --> 00:17:11.892
crystal chandeliers,

00:17:12.031 --> 00:17:14.522
wall-to-wall Italian marble.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:18.502
We'll take a drive up Michigan
Avenue in a vintage Duesenberg,

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:22.370
hobnob with the stars
of the silver screen,

00:17:22.441 --> 00:17:24.875
dance the Charleston
at a genuine speakeasy

00:17:24.943 --> 00:17:26.342
called the Green Mill.

00:17:26.412 --> 00:17:28.607
What do I wear?

00:17:30.816 --> 00:17:34.217
That's already taken care of.

00:17:34.286 --> 00:17:38.518
Our bags are packed and waiting
for us at the hotel.

00:17:40.926 --> 00:17:43.053
Champagne?

00:17:43.128 --> 00:17:44.720
It's on ice...

00:17:46.498 --> 00:17:48.022
in a silver bucket...

00:17:50.035 --> 00:17:52.799
right next to our canopy bed.

00:17:57.309 --> 00:17:58.571
B'Elanna?

00:17:59.978 --> 00:18:02.412
Doctor?

00:18:04.416 --> 00:18:06.884
Cortical stimulator.

00:18:06.985 --> 00:18:09.579
Initiate an iso-synaptic pulse.

00:18:12.291 --> 00:18:13.758
It's not working.

00:18:13.826 --> 00:18:15.123
Again!

00:18:17.362 --> 00:18:20.763
Increase the electrolytic levels
to 75 millijoules.

00:18:27.439 --> 00:18:29.771
We've lost her.

00:18:34.713 --> 00:18:37.079
Increasing electrolytic levels

00:18:37.149 --> 00:18:38.207
to 90 millijoules.

00:18:38.283 --> 00:18:40.251
There's nothing more we can do.

00:18:40.319 --> 00:18:43.482
Uh, maybe we can try
a direct neural resequencing.

00:18:43.555 --> 00:18:44.817
Lieutenant...

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:46.858
We can't just let her die!

00:18:47.926 --> 00:18:49.416
Return to your quarters.

00:18:49.495 --> 00:18:50.325
No!

00:18:54.166 --> 00:18:56.134
I don't want to leave her.

00:18:56.201 --> 00:18:57.600
I understand,

00:18:57.669 --> 00:19:00.763
but I need
to perform an analysis

00:19:00.839 --> 00:19:03.672
before her cells have
completely degraded.

00:19:03.742 --> 00:19:04.834
Please.

00:19:20.759 --> 00:19:22.693
Nine months, 28 days.

00:19:22.761 --> 00:19:24.786
We collected silicate
from a comet

00:19:24.863 --> 00:19:26.228
in the Podaris sector.

00:19:26.298 --> 00:19:28.323
According to Neelix's manifest,

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:30.925
those samples are stored
in the geology lab.

00:19:32.671 --> 00:19:35.868
They're showing no signs
of molecular degradation.

00:19:35.941 --> 00:19:37.670
Take us further back.

00:19:37.743 --> 00:19:39.734
Ten months, 11 days ago.

00:19:39.811 --> 00:19:42.006
Voyager was forced to land

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:44.514
on a Class-Y planetoid
in the Vaskan sector.

00:19:44.583 --> 00:19:46.244
The Demon-Class planet...

00:19:46.318 --> 00:19:48.809
one of our more
interesting missions.

00:19:48.887 --> 00:19:51.913
We set down looking
for deuterium and ended up

00:19:52.024 --> 00:19:54.083
helping a new form of life
to be born.

00:19:54.159 --> 00:19:56.024
The planet possessed
a biomimetic compound.

00:19:56.094 --> 00:19:57.618
The "silver blood."

00:19:57.696 --> 00:20:00.494
It sampled our DNA
and created duplicates

00:20:00.566 --> 00:20:01.863
of the entire crew.

00:20:01.934 --> 00:20:04.334
I've often wondered
what happened to them.

00:20:04.403 --> 00:20:05.768
Are they flourishing?

00:20:05.837 --> 00:20:07.930
Have they continued to evolve?

00:20:08.073 --> 00:20:09.768
Do they still resemble us?

00:20:16.515 --> 00:20:17.846
Is she?

00:20:17.916 --> 00:20:20.544
I'm afraid so.

00:20:20.619 --> 00:20:22.712
Scan for traces of deuterium,

00:20:22.788 --> 00:20:24.517
hydrogen sulfate
and dichromates.

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:25.921
Dichromates?

00:20:25.991 --> 00:20:27.185
Just do it.

00:20:32.864 --> 00:20:34.388
What's this about?

00:20:34.466 --> 00:20:37.401
We have a disturbing theory.

00:20:37.469 --> 00:20:39.528
I'm detecting
all of those compounds.

00:20:39.605 --> 00:20:42.199
I want you to inject her
with a dichromate catalyst.

00:20:42.274 --> 00:20:43.707
Commander?

00:20:43.775 --> 00:20:45.208
We've got to be sure.

00:21:04.296 --> 00:21:05.923
I don't understand.

00:21:06.064 --> 00:21:07.588
That wasn't B'Elanna.

00:21:07.666 --> 00:21:10.499
It was a duplicate...

00:21:10.569 --> 00:21:12.503
a biomimetic copy.

00:21:12.571 --> 00:21:14.129
Copy?

00:21:14.206 --> 00:21:16.572
We are all duplicates.

00:21:16.642 --> 00:21:19.042
None of us are real.

00:21:28.687 --> 00:21:31.850
Behold the primordial soup.

00:21:31.923 --> 00:21:33.447
That's what created us.

00:21:33.525 --> 00:21:34.549
Not just us.

00:21:34.626 --> 00:21:36.958
The entire ship is composed
of the same material.

00:21:37.095 --> 00:21:38.460
It's a biomimetic compound

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:41.465
that duplicated the crew's
molecular structure so precisely

00:21:41.533 --> 00:21:42.966
that I would never
have detected it

00:21:43.101 --> 00:21:45.069
if I hadn't known
what to look for.

00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:47.901
I was born on Earth...
in Indiana.

00:21:47.973 --> 00:21:49.531
I remember growing up there.

00:21:49.608 --> 00:21:51.974
I remember graduating
from the Academy.

00:21:52.044 --> 00:21:54.308
I have no memory
of being a copy.

00:21:54.379 --> 00:21:57.576
Apparently, the original
Kathryn Janeway's memories

00:21:57.649 --> 00:21:59.241
were duplicated as well.

00:21:59.318 --> 00:22:01.912
Somehow,
after the real Voyager left,

00:22:01.987 --> 00:22:05.286
we began to forget
we were duplicates.

00:22:05.357 --> 00:22:07.552
Eventually,
we assumed their lives

00:22:07.626 --> 00:22:09.253
and set a course for Earth.

00:22:10.562 --> 00:22:11.893
And now the warp core

00:22:11.963 --> 00:22:13.794
is breaking down
our cellular structure.

00:22:13.865 --> 00:22:16.663
We didn't think
the radiation would hurt us,

00:22:16.735 --> 00:22:18.100
because it isn't harmful
to humanoids.

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:19.762
Each and every one of you

00:22:19.838 --> 00:22:21.931
will disintegrate
just as B'Elanna did.

00:22:22.074 --> 00:22:23.598
I'm not immune, either.

00:22:23.675 --> 00:22:26.200
The holo-emitters, like
everything else, are copies.

00:22:26.278 --> 00:22:27.267
It's only a matter of time

00:22:27.346 --> 00:22:29.473
before my program begins
to degrade.

00:22:29.548 --> 00:22:30.947
What can we do
to stop the process?

00:22:31.083 --> 00:22:32.880
There is one option.

00:22:34.186 --> 00:22:35.380
Go back.

00:22:35.454 --> 00:22:37.718
To the Demon-Class planet?

00:22:37.789 --> 00:22:40.155
We were created
to survive there.

00:22:40.225 --> 00:22:41.852
He's correct.

00:22:41.927 --> 00:22:43.326
It's reasonable to assume

00:22:43.395 --> 00:22:45.329
that if we return
to our native environment,

00:22:45.397 --> 00:22:46.728
the degradation will cease.

00:22:48.533 --> 00:22:50.296
Even if we survived the trip,

00:22:50.369 --> 00:22:51.961
we'd be traveling thousands

00:22:52.104 --> 00:22:54.538
of light-years
in the wrong direction.

00:22:54.606 --> 00:22:56.164
It may be the only way.

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:00.375
Duplicate or not,

00:23:00.445 --> 00:23:02.470
I'm still the same person
I was yesterday,

00:23:02.547 --> 00:23:03.912
and so are all of you...

00:23:04.049 --> 00:23:06.574
and that means we're going
to do everything possible

00:23:06.651 --> 00:23:09.051
to complete our mission,
which is to reach Earth.

00:23:09.121 --> 00:23:10.088
Is that clear?

00:23:10.155 --> 00:23:11.918
- Yes, ma'am.
- I want you

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:13.514
to adjust
the environmental controls

00:23:13.592 --> 00:23:14.923
to simulate a Class-Y planet.

00:23:14.993 --> 00:23:16.722
That should slow the rate
of degradation.

00:23:16.795 --> 00:23:19.229
It's only a matter of time
before the environmental

00:23:19.297 --> 00:23:20.662
controls themselves
are affected.

00:23:20.732 --> 00:23:22.131
I realize that.

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:24.430
That's why we're going
to try and find a safe harbor

00:23:24.503 --> 00:23:26.733
till we can figure out a way
to stop the degradation.

00:23:26.805 --> 00:23:30.673
Scan for the nearest
Class-Y planet and set a course.

00:23:30.742 --> 00:23:31.936
In the meantime...

00:23:32.077 --> 00:23:34.875
I'll explain our situation
to the crew.

00:23:40.018 --> 00:23:42.350
There's still a great deal
we don't know

00:23:42.421 --> 00:23:43.820
about this phenomenon,

00:23:43.889 --> 00:23:47.222
and I have every confidence
we'll find a way to reverse it.

00:23:47.292 --> 00:23:49.351
So you're saying
all our experiences

00:23:49.428 --> 00:23:52.192
before we were duplicated...
none of it's real?

00:23:53.598 --> 00:23:56.795
I don't pretend to understand it
myself, Harry...

00:23:56.868 --> 00:24:00.201
but the way I choose
to look at it is this...

00:24:00.272 --> 00:24:03.070
if everything
about us was duplicated,

00:24:03.141 --> 00:24:05.837
that includes
our memory engrams,

00:24:05.911 --> 00:24:08.641
the emotional centers
of our brain.

00:24:08.713 --> 00:24:11.204
So, if you feel something...

00:24:11.283 --> 00:24:13.114
remember something...

00:24:13.185 --> 00:24:15.813
believe something...

00:24:15.887 --> 00:24:18.549
I'm not about to tell you
it's not real.

00:24:18.623 --> 00:24:21.922
But there is another crew
out there, right?

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:23.550
The real Voyager.

00:24:23.628 --> 00:24:26.495
I suppose there is,
but I don't want that thought

00:24:26.565 --> 00:24:28.897
to distract any of you
from our mission.

00:24:28.967 --> 00:24:30.764
What mission is that?

00:24:34.539 --> 00:24:36.769
The same
as it's always been, Tom...

00:24:36.842 --> 00:24:39.436
to reach the Alpha Quadrant
safe and sound,

00:24:39.511 --> 00:24:40.842
but to do that,

00:24:40.912 --> 00:24:43.676
we're going to have
to beat this problem...

00:24:45.250 --> 00:24:47.946
and for now,
that means conserving energy,

00:24:48.053 --> 00:24:52.217
running the ship in gray mode,
cutting crew shifts in half.

00:24:52.290 --> 00:24:56.420
The less you exert yourselves,
the slower the cellular decay.

00:24:59.164 --> 00:25:01.428
Duplicates or not...

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:03.593
you're still my crew.

00:25:03.668 --> 00:25:05.363
Dismissed.

00:25:09.574 --> 00:25:11.599
Tom...

00:25:11.676 --> 00:25:14.110
There's no one
here by that name.

00:25:14.179 --> 00:25:16.409
I just wanted to say...

00:25:16.481 --> 00:25:18.506
I'm sorry about B'Elanna.

00:25:18.583 --> 00:25:19.515
Sorry?

00:25:19.584 --> 00:25:20.551
What for?

00:25:20.619 --> 00:25:22.951
She was your wife.

00:25:24.389 --> 00:25:26.516
She was a duplicate...

00:25:26.591 --> 00:25:28.388
just like you are, Harry.

00:25:28.460 --> 00:25:29.825
You heard the Captain.

00:25:29.895 --> 00:25:31.556
If we're going to survive this,

00:25:31.630 --> 00:25:33.325
we've got to believe
in ourselves.

00:25:36.034 --> 00:25:38.400
You can drop
the good soldier routine.

00:25:38.470 --> 00:25:42.304
You don't have to do everything
the Captain says anymore.

00:25:42.374 --> 00:25:44.569
Hell, she's not
even the Captain.

00:25:44.643 --> 00:25:46.406
She is to me.

00:25:46.478 --> 00:25:50.278
Okay. Well, let's suppose
she does get us back to Earth.

00:25:50.348 --> 00:25:51.337
What then?

00:25:51.416 --> 00:25:53.407
You really think your family

00:25:53.485 --> 00:25:56.249
is going to welcome
you with open arms?

00:25:56.321 --> 00:25:57.948
I don't know.

00:25:58.056 --> 00:25:59.853
For all you know,
the real Harry Kim

00:25:59.925 --> 00:26:02.189
is having Sunday dinner
with them right now.

00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:04.319
And you come strolling
through the door,

00:26:04.396 --> 00:26:05.761
they're going to see you

00:26:05.830 --> 00:26:08.094
for exactly what you
are... an impostor.

00:26:08.166 --> 00:26:10.396
So what are we going to do, huh?

00:26:10.468 --> 00:26:13.062
Wait around
till we all disintegrate?

00:26:26.384 --> 00:26:27.851
Come in.

00:26:29.387 --> 00:26:33.016
Chicken paprikash...
my grandmother's recipe.

00:26:33.091 --> 00:26:37.790
Well, maybe not my grandmother,
but it's still delicious.

00:26:37.862 --> 00:26:39.887
It's our weekly dinner together.

00:26:39.965 --> 00:26:41.523
Don't tell me you forgot.

00:26:42.601 --> 00:26:44.933
We've lost three more people.

00:26:45.036 --> 00:26:46.867
We've got to head back.

00:26:49.407 --> 00:26:52.501
I've spent the past five years
trying to get this crew home.

00:26:52.577 --> 00:26:54.408
I'm not about to quit now.

00:26:54.479 --> 00:26:55.878
Listen to yourself.

00:26:55.947 --> 00:26:58.381
You haven't even been alive
for five years.

00:26:58.450 --> 00:27:00.645
Home is a Class-Y planet
in the Delta Quadrant.

00:27:00.719 --> 00:27:02.550
We don't belong on Earth.

00:27:02.621 --> 00:27:04.282
How do you know where we belong?

00:27:04.356 --> 00:27:05.789
For all we know,

00:27:05.857 --> 00:27:07.290
the real Voyager's
been destroyed

00:27:07.359 --> 00:27:08.792
and we're all that's left.

00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:10.623
For all we know,

00:27:10.695 --> 00:27:13.596
we're supposed
to be living their lives.

00:27:13.665 --> 00:27:15.530
That's a pretty big
assumption...

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:17.761
and it's putting this crew
in danger.

00:27:21.139 --> 00:27:23.505
There's only one thing
I know how to be, Chakotay,

00:27:23.575 --> 00:27:25.634
and that's Kathryn Janeway.

00:27:25.710 --> 00:27:26.642
I'd like to think

00:27:26.711 --> 00:27:28.372
I know Captain Janeway
pretty well myself,

00:27:28.446 --> 00:27:30.641
and as much as she'd like
to get her crew home,

00:27:30.715 --> 00:27:34.481
I don't think she'd be willing
to kill them in the process.

00:27:37.722 --> 00:27:41.158
Maybe this dinner wasn't
such a good idea after all.

00:27:52.504 --> 00:27:54.597
I've tried everything
I can think of...

00:27:54.673 --> 00:27:56.732
bio-molecular enhancers,

00:27:56.808 --> 00:27:58.935
gene splicing
with replicated DNA...

00:27:59.010 --> 00:28:01.638
and I'm no closer
to finding a cure.

00:28:01.713 --> 00:28:03.305
But I do have an idea.

00:28:03.381 --> 00:28:04.313
I'm listening.

00:28:04.382 --> 00:28:06.009
Find the original Voyager.

00:28:06.084 --> 00:28:07.642
If the real Captain Janeway
were here,

00:28:07.719 --> 00:28:09.380
we could sample her DNA

00:28:09.454 --> 00:28:11.513
and imprint it
onto your mimetic pattern.

00:28:11.589 --> 00:28:13.819
But, Doctor, we have no way
of knowing where they are.

00:28:13.892 --> 00:28:16.087
They could be behind
us, ahead of us,

00:28:16.161 --> 00:28:17.788
back on Earth...
destroyed.

00:28:17.862 --> 00:28:20.888
Besides, even if we could
find the real Janeway,

00:28:20.965 --> 00:28:22.660
how do we know she'd help?

00:28:22.734 --> 00:28:24.326
She's you.

00:28:25.603 --> 00:28:27.332
My emitter's
starting to degrade.

00:28:27.405 --> 00:28:29.339
You better get back to Sick Bay.

00:28:29.407 --> 00:28:30.339
Tuvok to the Captain.

00:28:30.408 --> 00:28:32.899
Sensors have detected
a Class-Y planet.

00:28:32.977 --> 00:28:35.070
On my way.

00:28:35.146 --> 00:28:37.637
It may not be home,
but it checks out.

00:28:37.716 --> 00:28:38.910
Thermionic radiation...

00:28:39.050 --> 00:28:41.678
surface temperatures in
excess of 500 kelvins.

00:28:41.753 --> 00:28:44.722
Just what the Doctor ordered.

00:28:44.789 --> 00:28:46.416
Safe harbor?

00:28:46.491 --> 00:28:49.085
There's no guarantee
this is going to work.

00:28:50.762 --> 00:28:55.222
Harry, vent all plasma
from the nacelles.

00:28:55.300 --> 00:28:58.531
Transfer available power
to atmospheric thrusters

00:28:58.603 --> 00:29:00.400
and stand by to commence
landing sequence.

00:29:00.472 --> 00:29:02.372
Yes, ma'am.

00:29:02.440 --> 00:29:03.964
Red Alert.

00:29:04.042 --> 00:29:06.135
Landing struts on line.

00:29:06.211 --> 00:29:08.145
Inertial dampers at maximum.

00:29:08.213 --> 00:29:10.408
Take us down, Mr. Paris.

00:29:11.449 --> 00:29:13.212
Captain, a vessel is approaching

00:29:13.284 --> 00:29:14.717
from the planet's surface.

00:29:14.786 --> 00:29:16.515
On screen.

00:29:16.588 --> 00:29:18.579
They're hailing.

00:29:18.656 --> 00:29:20.351
Open a channel.

00:29:20.425 --> 00:29:24.885
You're in direct violation
of the Ord'Mirit Mining Treaty.

00:29:24.996 --> 00:29:27.226
Leave orbit
or you'll be destroyed.

00:29:29.334 --> 00:29:30.926
They are firing weapons.

00:29:53.091 --> 00:29:55.116
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:29:55.193 --> 00:29:57.889
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:29:57.962 --> 00:30:00.556
We are not your enemy.

00:30:02.133 --> 00:30:03.566
They seem to disagree.

00:30:03.635 --> 00:30:06.399
We're not interested
in your mining operation.

00:30:06.471 --> 00:30:07.904
Our ship is badly damaged.

00:30:07.972 --> 00:30:10.941
We need to set down
on the surface to make repairs.

00:30:11.075 --> 00:30:14.044
We repeat:
Leave or be destroyed.

00:30:15.547 --> 00:30:17.777
Shields down to 52 percent.

00:30:17.849 --> 00:30:19.407
With our systems degrading,

00:30:19.484 --> 00:30:22.044
we won't be able
to take this much longer.

00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:24.850
Target their weapon systems.

00:30:24.923 --> 00:30:25.890
Fire.

00:30:27.425 --> 00:30:28.790
No effect.

00:30:30.195 --> 00:30:32.322
Hull breaches
on Decks 11, 14 and 15.

00:30:32.397 --> 00:30:35.798
The damaged sections are turning
into biomimetic matter.

00:30:35.867 --> 00:30:37.300
Containment fields are failing.

00:30:37.368 --> 00:30:39.131
Evacuate those decks.

00:30:39.204 --> 00:30:42.071
If we emit a polaron burst,
we can disable their shields

00:30:42.140 --> 00:30:43.835
long enough to target
their warp core.

00:30:43.908 --> 00:30:46.274
No. We're not going
to destroy them

00:30:46.344 --> 00:30:47.971
over a misunderstanding.

00:30:48.079 --> 00:30:50.013
Either that or retreat.

00:30:55.086 --> 00:30:56.815
We're Starfleet officers.

00:30:56.888 --> 00:30:58.355
We can't forget that.

00:30:58.423 --> 00:31:00.254
Break orbit.

00:31:00.325 --> 00:31:03.158
That planet may be our
last chance for survival.

00:31:03.228 --> 00:31:05.321
We'll have to find
another option.

00:31:05.396 --> 00:31:08.456
I'm not sure why we're
still taking orders from you.

00:31:08.533 --> 00:31:10.660
Lieutenant, follow orders
or leave the Bridge.

00:31:16.007 --> 00:31:18.168
The alien vessel's not pursuing.

00:31:18.243 --> 00:31:21.644
Begin scanning
for other Class-Y planets.

00:31:21.713 --> 00:31:26.343
Harry, transmit a distress call
on all subspace bands.

00:31:26.417 --> 00:31:28.282
If the real Voyager
is out there,

00:31:28.353 --> 00:31:29.945
I want to find them.

00:31:30.054 --> 00:31:31.282
In the meantime,

00:31:31.356 --> 00:31:34.382
which direction
do you want me to go?

00:31:35.827 --> 00:31:39.228
Resume course for the Alpha
Quadrant, Mr. Paris.

00:31:50.308 --> 00:31:53.471
I know what you're going to say
and I don't want to hear it.

00:31:53.544 --> 00:31:54.977
Too bad.

00:31:55.079 --> 00:31:57.343
I'm willing to take a
little insolence from Tom,

00:31:57.415 --> 00:31:58.973
but I shouldn't have
to remind you

00:31:59.083 --> 00:32:00.345
that I'm still the Captain.

00:32:00.418 --> 00:32:01.680
You're not.

00:32:01.753 --> 00:32:04.745
You're a biomimetic life-form
created in her image.

00:32:04.822 --> 00:32:07.916
Are you saying you're not taking
orders from me anymore?

00:32:08.059 --> 00:32:09.822
I'm saying
you need to step back

00:32:09.894 --> 00:32:13.091
and look at our situation
objectively.

00:32:13.164 --> 00:32:15.132
You think I should
have given the order

00:32:15.199 --> 00:32:16.393
to fire on that vessel.

00:32:16.467 --> 00:32:19.527
No. I agreed with your
decision to stand down,

00:32:19.604 --> 00:32:22.630
but how long can we adhere
to Starfleet principles

00:32:22.707 --> 00:32:24.698
before we start making
compromises?

00:32:24.776 --> 00:32:26.767
As long as it takes.

00:32:26.844 --> 00:32:29.506
Our ship may be deteriorating,

00:32:29.580 --> 00:32:32.105
but our humanity is intact.

00:32:32.183 --> 00:32:34.947
Belief alone won't hold
this ship together.

00:32:35.086 --> 00:32:36.678
It's gotten us this far.

00:32:36.754 --> 00:32:38.244
Not far enough.

00:32:39.590 --> 00:32:43.048
Tom and I aren't the only ones
who question your decisions.

00:32:43.127 --> 00:32:44.355
Now that the truth is known,

00:32:44.429 --> 00:32:46.556
a lot of people think
we should turn around

00:32:46.631 --> 00:32:48.258
and head for the Class-Y planet.

00:32:48.333 --> 00:32:51.268
They're starting to remember
their existence before Voyager.

00:32:51.336 --> 00:32:52.803
What?

00:32:52.870 --> 00:32:56.601
What existence?

00:32:56.674 --> 00:32:59.108
Pools of biomimetic fluid?

00:32:59.177 --> 00:33:01.737
We didn't even experience
sentience

00:33:01.813 --> 00:33:03.576
until Voyager came along.

00:33:03.648 --> 00:33:05.013
What good is sentience

00:33:05.083 --> 00:33:07.517
if we're not alive
to experience it?

00:33:07.585 --> 00:33:10.110
Kathryn, we've got to go back.

00:33:10.188 --> 00:33:13.123
I promised the crew
I'd get them home.

00:33:13.191 --> 00:33:15.625
Home isn't Earth.

00:33:21.366 --> 00:33:25.325
Janeway to Sick Bay.
Medical emergency.

00:33:27.805 --> 00:33:28.863
He's not responding.

00:33:31.576 --> 00:33:34.044
His neural pathways
are destabilizing.

00:33:55.666 --> 00:33:58.635
We've lost Commander Chakotay.

00:34:00.271 --> 00:34:03.206
Duplicate or not,
he was real to me...

00:34:06.144 --> 00:34:09.341
and he was
a fine Starfleet officer.

00:34:09.414 --> 00:34:10.779
And...

00:34:16.654 --> 00:34:18.246
he was a friend...

00:34:19.724 --> 00:34:20.918
who...

00:34:22.393 --> 00:34:25.294
wasn't afraid to let me know
when I am wrong.

00:34:28.966 --> 00:34:30.126
Mr. Kim,

00:34:30.201 --> 00:34:33.967
bring the enhanced
warp drive on line.

00:34:37.975 --> 00:34:39.465
Turn Voyager around.

00:34:41.913 --> 00:34:43.710
We're going home.

00:34:43.781 --> 00:34:45.646
Captain...

00:34:47.085 --> 00:34:48.518
Set a course...

00:34:50.254 --> 00:34:52.085
for the Demon planet.

00:35:05.903 --> 00:35:07.803
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:35:07.872 --> 00:35:12.070
We've lost 63 crewmen, and our
systems are continuing to fail.

00:35:12.143 --> 00:35:15.044
Though we're still five weeks
away from the Demon planet,

00:35:15.113 --> 00:35:16.876
we haven't given up hope.

00:35:16.948 --> 00:35:18.643
The holographic projectors
in Sick Bay

00:35:18.716 --> 00:35:21.082
went off-line at 0300.

00:35:21.152 --> 00:35:23.211
We've lost the Doctor.

00:35:24.589 --> 00:35:26.523
What's Tom's condition?

00:35:26.591 --> 00:35:28.491
No change.

00:35:28.559 --> 00:35:30.493
Well... hmm...

00:35:30.561 --> 00:35:33.587
Iooks like we're in the market
for a new medical officer.

00:35:33.664 --> 00:35:35.325
Feel up to it, Neelix?

00:35:37.735 --> 00:35:40.203
I've only been trained
as a field medic.

00:35:40.271 --> 00:35:42.000
It'll have to do.

00:35:43.074 --> 00:35:45.542
What about my other duties?

00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:48.579
Make Sick Bay your priority.

00:35:50.348 --> 00:35:52.646
At this point...

00:35:52.717 --> 00:35:54.344
morale is a luxury.

00:35:54.418 --> 00:35:56.750
How's the core holding up?

00:35:56.821 --> 00:35:58.186
The modified nanoprobes are

00:35:58.256 --> 00:35:59.951
still reinforcing
the warp field.

00:36:00.024 --> 00:36:03.187
It should remain functioning
until we reach the Demon planet.

00:36:03.261 --> 00:36:05.593
However, there is less
than a 20 percent probability

00:36:05.663 --> 00:36:07.858
that Voyager will remain intact
that long.

00:36:10.334 --> 00:36:12.097
Well...

00:36:12.170 --> 00:36:15.230
it won't be the first time
this crew has been...

00:36:17.141 --> 00:36:18.130
up against...

00:36:18.209 --> 00:36:19.904
Captain?

00:36:20.044 --> 00:36:22.638
It's all right. I'm just...

00:36:24.215 --> 00:36:26.615
a little tired.

00:36:26.684 --> 00:36:28.743
Let Ensign Kim
take command for a while.

00:36:28.819 --> 00:36:30.787
I'm still the Captain.

00:36:30.855 --> 00:36:34.484
And I am
the Chief Medical Officer.

00:36:34.559 --> 00:36:38.120
Don't force me
to relieve you of your duties.

00:36:38.196 --> 00:36:43.133
Your concerns have been noted...
sir.

00:36:51.909 --> 00:36:54.002
Now...

00:36:55.746 --> 00:36:58.510
there is another matter.

00:36:58.583 --> 00:37:02.041
I want to download
the ship's database...

00:37:02.119 --> 00:37:05.816
and our personal logs
into a signal beacon.

00:37:08.392 --> 00:37:10.451
In the event we don't survive,

00:37:10.528 --> 00:37:14.487
there should be some record
of our accomplishments.

00:37:14.565 --> 00:37:16.260
A time capsule.

00:37:18.302 --> 00:37:21.294
This crew's existence
may have been brief...

00:37:22.807 --> 00:37:25.139
but it's been distinguished.

00:37:28.079 --> 00:37:30.547
None of you...

00:37:33.584 --> 00:37:36.052
deserves to be forgotten.

00:37:39.490 --> 00:37:42.789
I will use unaffected components
to construct a beacon.

00:38:00.645 --> 00:38:03.011
The deflector's off-line.

00:38:03.080 --> 00:38:06.345
Interstellar dust is
contaminating the warp field.

00:38:06.417 --> 00:38:07.748
Purge it.

00:38:07.818 --> 00:38:09.115
I can't.

00:38:09.186 --> 00:38:11.313
The exhaust manifolds
have disintegrated.

00:38:15.393 --> 00:38:18.556
We've come too far
to be stopped by dust.

00:38:20.631 --> 00:38:23.191
Reroute auxiliary power
to the deflector.

00:38:24.235 --> 00:38:26.897
Warp field failure in eight...

00:38:26.971 --> 00:38:28.029
seven...

00:38:28.105 --> 00:38:29.037
six...

00:38:29.106 --> 00:38:30.596
five...

00:38:30.675 --> 00:38:31.767
four...

00:38:31.842 --> 00:38:33.139
three...

00:38:33.210 --> 00:38:34.268
Got it.

00:38:34.345 --> 00:38:38.406
Reinitializing the deflector.

00:38:38.482 --> 00:38:41.007
The warp field has stabilized.

00:38:44.188 --> 00:38:46.679
I may not be
morale officer anymore,

00:38:46.757 --> 00:38:49.920
but I think this is
a cause for celebration.

00:38:49.994 --> 00:38:51.859
What do you say, Captain?

00:38:55.599 --> 00:38:57.123
Captain?

00:39:08.112 --> 00:39:09.773
She's gone.

00:39:24.228 --> 00:39:28.995
Acting Captain's Log,
Stardate 52597.4.

00:39:29.066 --> 00:39:33.628
Our situation's getting worse
every day.

00:39:33.704 --> 00:39:36.434
More than 80 percent
of the ship is uninhabitable.

00:39:36.507 --> 00:39:38.441
Most of the crew are gone.

00:39:38.509 --> 00:39:40.602
It seems less and less likely
that the few of us left

00:39:40.678 --> 00:39:41.804
will reach our destination.

00:39:52.723 --> 00:39:55.248
Computer, hull status.

00:39:55.326 --> 00:39:58.591
Hull integrity at 45 percent.

00:40:00.231 --> 00:40:02.028
What was that?

00:40:02.099 --> 00:40:05.193
Cargo Bay 2 has decompressed.

00:40:05.269 --> 00:40:08.033
Seal off that deck.

00:40:13.611 --> 00:40:17.707
Computer, erect a level-10
force field around the Bridge.

00:40:17.782 --> 00:40:19.113
Unable to comply.

00:40:19.183 --> 00:40:20.878
Seven...

00:40:20.951 --> 00:40:22.316
I need more power up here.

00:40:22.386 --> 00:40:24.047
The bulkheads are coming apart.

00:40:24.121 --> 00:40:26.453
I'm transferring the last
of our power reserves.

00:40:30.394 --> 00:40:33.192
Deck 1 force field is in place.

00:40:34.565 --> 00:40:35.964
That's better.

00:40:36.100 --> 00:40:37.362
How's life support?

00:40:37.435 --> 00:40:38.800
Degrading.

00:40:38.869 --> 00:40:41.133
We have approximately
ten hours of air remaining.

00:40:41.205 --> 00:40:44.140
What about the time capsule?

00:40:44.208 --> 00:40:45.800
It's ready for launch.

00:40:47.745 --> 00:40:49.178
Do it.

00:40:54.618 --> 00:40:56.916
The launch sequencer
has misfired.

00:40:56.987 --> 00:40:58.978
Reset the initiator;
try it again.

00:41:00.057 --> 00:41:00.989
It won't work.

00:41:01.125 --> 00:41:03.559
The launch mechanism is
demolecularized.

00:41:03.627 --> 00:41:05.322
Salvage the probe.

00:41:07.364 --> 00:41:09.389
It's too late.

00:41:09.467 --> 00:41:11.025
It's been destroyed.

00:41:12.670 --> 00:41:15.138
Personal logs...

00:41:15.206 --> 00:41:17.037
mission logs...

00:41:17.107 --> 00:41:19.041
all our history...

00:41:19.109 --> 00:41:21.168
gone.

00:41:22.646 --> 00:41:24.238
Now what?

00:41:25.816 --> 00:41:27.647
I'm detecting a vessel...

00:41:27.718 --> 00:41:29.242
22 light-years away.

00:41:36.260 --> 00:41:37.750
I see it.

00:41:42.666 --> 00:41:45.863
I'm trying to hail them.

00:41:45.936 --> 00:41:48.234
The subspace transceiver's
malfunctioning.

00:41:49.940 --> 00:41:52.340
If they move out of range,
they won't see us.

00:41:53.777 --> 00:41:55.540
We still have
one active com circuit,

00:41:55.613 --> 00:41:57.740
but we'll have to go
to impulse to use it.

00:41:57.815 --> 00:41:59.282
Seven, drop out of warp.

00:41:59.350 --> 00:42:01.818
The engine controls are fused.

00:42:01.886 --> 00:42:02.784
Then unfuse them.

00:42:02.853 --> 00:42:05.947
Without an isolytic converter,
I cannot comply.

00:42:07.024 --> 00:42:08.423
Dump the core.

00:42:08.492 --> 00:42:10.483
Ensign, dropping out of warp
at this velocity

00:42:10.561 --> 00:42:11.721
could tear the ship apart.

00:42:11.795 --> 00:42:13.490
We're already falling apart.

00:42:13.564 --> 00:42:15.156
We're not going to make it

00:42:15.232 --> 00:42:17.291
to the Class-Y planet
in one piece,

00:42:17.368 --> 00:42:20.565
which means that ship is
our only hope.

00:42:22.072 --> 00:42:23.471
Think about it.

00:42:25.242 --> 00:42:27.802
What would Captain Janeway
have done?

00:42:30.581 --> 00:42:34.142
Computer, prepare to eject
the warp core.

00:42:34.218 --> 00:42:37.949
Authorization: Seven of Nine-
omega-phi-nine-three.

00:42:38.022 --> 00:42:39.956
Warp ejection systems enabled.

00:42:42.526 --> 00:42:44.153
Eject the core.

00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:52.935
We've lost
attitude control and shields.

00:42:53.003 --> 00:42:55.096
Hull integrity at 19 percent.

00:42:57.207 --> 00:42:59.141
Reroute life support!

00:42:59.209 --> 00:43:00.608
Hell, reroute everything
we've got left

00:43:00.678 --> 00:43:01.667
to the containment fields.

00:43:07.184 --> 00:43:10.347
Hull breaches
on Decks 9, 10 and 11.

00:43:13.591 --> 00:43:14.888
Seven.

00:43:14.959 --> 00:43:15.948
Seven!

00:43:19.229 --> 00:43:20.696
Computer...

00:43:20.764 --> 00:43:23.324
how long until we're within
hailing range of that ship?

00:43:23.400 --> 00:43:25.925
F-f-f-five minutes
and 30 seconds.

00:43:26.036 --> 00:43:28.561
F-f-f-five minutes and
30 seconds.

00:43:34.979 --> 00:43:36.913
Range?

00:43:36.981 --> 00:43:38.676
Five million kilometers.

00:43:38.749 --> 00:43:41.149
Try hailing again.

00:43:42.419 --> 00:43:44.353
No response.

00:43:44.421 --> 00:43:46.912
Captain, I've found the source
of the distress call.

00:43:46.991 --> 00:43:48.151
It's coming from a vessel.

00:43:48.225 --> 00:43:49.351
Can you identify it?

00:43:49.426 --> 00:43:51.189
No. The readings are erratic.

00:43:51.261 --> 00:43:53.593
Looks like they've taken
heavy damage.

00:43:53.664 --> 00:43:55.495
400,000 kilometers.

00:43:55.566 --> 00:43:57.557
Drop to impulse.
Are the rescue teams ready?

00:43:59.103 --> 00:44:01.298
Bridge to Sick Bay.
Stand by for casualties.

00:44:01.372 --> 00:44:02.703
In visual range.

00:44:02.773 --> 00:44:04.104
On screen.

00:44:08.512 --> 00:44:09.706
Where's the ship?

00:44:10.781 --> 00:44:12.009
No sign of it.

00:44:12.082 --> 00:44:14.346
That debris... that couldn't be
all that's left.

00:44:14.418 --> 00:44:18.149
I'm detecting residual
deuterium, antineutrons,

00:44:18.222 --> 00:44:19.917
traces of dichromates.

00:44:20.057 --> 00:44:23.083
If it was a vessel,
it isn't anymore.

00:44:23.160 --> 00:44:25.685
Scan for life signs,
escape pods.

00:44:26.764 --> 00:44:28.254
None.

00:44:35.172 --> 00:44:37.265
Make a note
in the ship's record...

00:44:37.341 --> 00:44:40.936
we received a distress
call at 0900 hours.

00:44:41.011 --> 00:44:44.538
Arrived at the vessel's
last known coordinates at 2120.

00:44:48.485 --> 00:44:50.953
The ship was destroyed.

00:44:51.055 --> 00:44:52.682
Cause unknown.

00:44:54.591 --> 00:44:56.616
No survivors.

00:44:58.929 --> 00:45:00.863
Mr. Paris, resume course.

00:45:00.931 --> 00:45:02.125
Aye, sir.
